#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""caf-art — a reactive ANSI coffee scene for `caf`.

A procedurally drawn cup of coffee rendered with half-block characters at 2x
vertical resolution, steam rendered in braille (2x4 dots per cell) driven by a
curl-noise particle simulation, and a shallow-water height-field simulation for
the liquid surface — sipping, stirring, refilling, and CPU heat all disturb the
same physical surface. Only changed lines are re-emitted each frame, and the
layout recomputes from the terminal size every frame.

The cup is also a rigid body: real IMU tilt (M2+ MacBooks) slants the liquid,
and past ~15 degrees it runs over the rim, streaks down the cup, stains the
saucer, and pools on the floor against the terminal walls. Tip further (or
shove hard) and the cup slides off the saucer, tumbles, bounces off the
window edges, and shatters coffee everywhere — housekeeping restores order a
few seconds later. The ambient light sensor dims the scene with the room.

Interactive keys while running:
  s      take a sip (refills with a pour animation when the cup runs low)
  space  stir the coffee
  x      nudge the cup (careful)
  w      steam writes the current time
  t      cycle themes
  q      quit (Ctrl+C also works)

Flags:
  --pomodoro N   the coffee IS the timer: drains over N minutes of work,
                 rings and refills for a 5-minute break, repeats
  --weather      fetch local weather once; rain/snow/sun ambience
  --zen          screensaver mode: no status line, slow theme crossfades,
                 occasional automatic stirs
  --hires        render as real images via the kitty graphics protocol
                 (Ghostty/kitty); falls back to ANSI elsewhere
  --3d           ray-marched SDF cup with soft shadows, a reflective liquid,
                 and volumetric steam that orbits with the camera
  --sound        procedural foley (clink/glug/slurp/chime/crash) via afplay

User themes: ~/.config/caf/themes.toml, e.g.
  [mytheme]
  icon = "🍫"
  name = "Mocha"
  cup = [180, 130, 90]
  liquid = [60, 35, 20]
  crema = [190, 150, 110]
  steam = [235, 230, 225]
  saucer = [140, 95, 60]

Runs `caffeinate -d` for as long as it's on screen.
"""

